{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vnygxstilvqdisp7apg5frigxzdl2yvlorgso3xkovamruylqgda","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. The Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte on every configuration tested.\n\n## Result\n\n**No divergences found in the Rust translation** — it was already faithful. `cargo check` was clean, and all 54 differential tests pass.\n\n### Artifacts (`translation/`)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | 11 C symbols → 11 Rust symbols, `nm -D` diff **EMPTY**; 0 unresolved project symbols |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 29 rejection rows, all checked |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 24 configuration rows, all checked |\n| `tests/common/mod.rs` | libloading harness — **both** `.so`s loaded via `dlopen`/`dlsym`, SplitMix64 PRNG, field-wise bit-exact `ResultArray` comparison |\n| `tests/phase_b_configs.rs` | 24 tests (C1–C24) |\n| `tests/phase_c_errors.rs` | 28 tests (E1, E3–E29) |\n| `tests/phase_d_symbols.rs` | 2 tests — automated `nm -D` parity gate |\n| `run_all_combos.sh` | enumerates features from Cargo.toml, runs suite × 2 profiles |\n\n### One genuine finding (a C-side trap, documented not \"fixed\")\n`modulo_operation(INT32_MIN, -1, _, _)`: the C compiles `%` to `idivl`, whose quotient overflows → `#DE` → **SIGFPE**. Verified with a C driver linked against the C `.so`: `exit=136`. The C returns no value, so there is nothing to compare; Rust's `wrapping_rem` yields `0`. Excluded from value comparisons and documented in `ERRORS.md`. It is **unreachable through every composed path** — `process_with_foreach`/`arrayfunc` always pass `item->rank` (always `0..=9`) as `b`.\n\n### Coverage highlights\n- **Low-level entry points driven directly**, not just `arrayfunc`: manual `init` → 4× `process_with_foreach` → `compute_weighted_sum` → `compare` chain, with the full 248-byte struct diffed **after every stage** (C19/C20).\n- **Function-pointer trace equality** (C16): the same Rust `extern \"C\"` op is handed to both libraries and the per-call `(a,b,unused1,unused2)` traces are compared — proving C and Rust invoke `operation_func` identically.\n- `safe_double_to_int` over 30 000 arbitrary 64-bit patterns plus every clamp boundary, `nextafter` on both sides, sNaN/qNaN/negative-NaN payloads, subnormals, `±0.0`.\n- Negative and `INT32_MIN` indices into `compare_results_in_array` (C only bounds-checks the *upper* limit) — address-wrapping arithmetic matches.\n- **Negative control performed**: injecting a one-value bug into `add_operation` made 3 tests fail with exact diagnostics, confirming the harness is not vacuously passing.\n\n### Gate status\n- [x] Symbol diff empty, 0 undefined project symbols\n- [x] All 24 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass over randomized inputs — plus **10 extra seeds** via `DIFF_SEED=<n>`, all green\n- [x] No binary target exists (`CMakeLists.txt` has only `add_library`; no `[[bin]]`) — stdout gate N/A\n- [x] All 29 `ERRORS.md` rows have passing tests\n- [x] Green under all feature combos (crate declares no `[features]`, so default ≡ `--no-default-features`, both run) × debug **and** release\n\n`c_src/` unmodified (source md5s unchanged; only the prescribed `build/` dir added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3225,"cache_read_input_tokens":98152,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3225,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03c5f30a-92c3-4d93-826d-e222e5e8b692","uuid":"7d9f95b6-5b33-4210-93cd-2249a5573ea0","timestamp":"2026-09-05T13:12:41.126Z"}
